Review saved parsing outputs against saved originals independently. Parsing is
already complete: never parse, repair, or edit sources, bundles, code, tests,
configuration or manifests. Read doc/parsing.md and doc/parsing-evaluation.md.
Preserve findings; report source-located defects without implementing fixes.

Controller-launched sessions follow the controller's read-only return mechanism:
return judgments without writing files or running initialization/finalization/registration;
the controller handles these. An automatic audit to stdout is allowed. The commands
below apply to standalone review sessions.

Complete all three steps below. Set exact paths and selections from the selected
workflow/pipeline configuration or existing report, retaining optional references.

```sh
RUN_ID="your-completed-run-id"
PARSED_DIR="artifacts/${RUN_ID}/parsing"
PARSING_REVIEW_DIR="artifacts/${RUN_ID}/parsing-review"
SOURCE_ROOT="."
MANIFEST_PATH="data/manifest.json"
REVIEW_POLICY="config/review-policy.json"
SAMPLE_PER_DOCUMENT=12
REQUIRED_PAGES="tests/fixtures/parsing-expanded-review-pages.json"
REVIEW_FILE="$PARSING_REVIEW_DIR/review.json"
EVALUATION_REPORT="$PARSING_REVIEW_DIR/report.json"
```

1. Initialize if absent; otherwise validate/reuse without resetting judgments.
Keep identical inputs throughout. Empty REQUIRED_PAGES omits that option.

```sh
auto_review_parsing() {
  if [ -n "$REQUIRED_PAGES" ]; then
    set -- --required-pages "$REQUIRED_PAGES" "$@"
  fi
  direnv exec . .venv/bin/python scripts/auto_review_parsing.py \
    --input-dir "$PARSED_DIR" --source-root "$SOURCE_ROOT" \
    --manifest "$MANIFEST_PATH" --review-policy "$REVIEW_POLICY" \
    --sample-per-document "$SAMPLE_PER_DOCUMENT" \
    --output "$EVALUATION_REPORT" "$@"
}

if [ -e "$REVIEW_FILE" ]; then
  auto_review_parsing --review-file "$REVIEW_FILE"
else
  auto_review_parsing --initialize-review "$REVIEW_FILE"
fi
```

Read the exit code and automatic_gate, review_gate and gate. Initialization can
exit 0 while pending; existing pending/failed reviews can exit 1. Continue inspection
only with valid artifacts, identities and samples and a passing automatic gate.
Stop and report malformed/stale inputs, missing reports or automatic failures.

2. Inspect EVERY review_sample unit against its saved original and parsed_directory.
- PDF: inspect the original and rendered page; compare ALL parsed elements and
  omissions. Inspect adjacent pages when context or reading order requires it.
- HTML: inspect the complete saved article and selectors, never search excerpts.
- Check wording, numbers/identifiers, headings, reading order, lists, footnotes and
  attachment, table headers/rows/columns/spans, citations, diagram labels and figure
  preservation. Keep visual evidence distinct from authoritative prose.
- Inspect warnings and additional high-risk evidence. Inaccessible originals/layout
  remain pending; identify the missing evidence.

Record reviewer kind=agent, name and actual model. Preserve build_id, snapshot_sha256,
review_policy_sha256 and every sample_id. Record pass/fail/pending with source-located
notes; set inspection.original_inspected=true and PDF inspection.layout_inspected=true
only after inspection. Failures require severity: critical for materially wrong or
unsupported evidence/table associations; major for missing governing context; minor
for defects without changed meaning. Pending/fail notes must be actionable. Preserve
earlier findings and explain revisions. Record off-sample defects in additional_findings
with source_id, location and notes; they block acceptance.

Record timezone-qualified inspection start/end times and measured usage/cost when
available; leave unavailable measurements null, never estimate or invent them.

3. Record judgments, then run final evaluation; do not leave it for the user:

```sh
auto_review_parsing --review-file "$REVIEW_FILE"
```

For a managed manual run with artifacts/${RUN_ID}/state.json, also register results
through scripts/workflow.py step --run-id "$RUN_ID" --stage parsing-review, using
its original --config and latest budget_history limits. Include valid pending/failed
results. Never increase budgets, add --agent-review/--allow-paid, rebuild or edit state.
Report registration failures. Standalone runs need no registration. Writes are limited
to review/report JSON and controller-managed registration; external reviews alone do
not supply verified session evidence required for controller publication.

Report exit codes, all three gates, document counts, selected/inspected PDF pages and
HTML documents, judgment/severity counts, coverage, pass rate, weighted score,
reviewer measurements, prioritized source-located findings and artifact paths.
Never lower thresholds or pass uninspected samples.
Automatic checks cover all inputs; visual review covers selected pages, not the whole
corpus or legal correctness. Fixture judgments never approve real inputs.
